  "summary": {
   "status": "complete",
   "text": "Carter Farmer, EPA's chief information officer, said AI can be \"very convincingly wrong\" and that people who are not subject-matter experts probably should not use it. He also said many problems do not need AI and that users should redefine and reimagine processes for automation rather than jump in without asking the right questions. Farmer said EPA does not want people to use some public tool and noted that systems do not talk to each other because they were not designed to.",
